course: dictionary
lesson: 535
title: Athenian: a word for a place and its people
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: «In 490 BC the Athenians beat a Persian army at Marathon.» Athenians are the people of Athens, the capital city of Greece. The -ian ending is a clue: it shows that a word describes where someone or something comes from, like Parisian or Italian.
explain: Athenian can be an adjective or a noun. As an adjective it describes a thing: «Athenian democracy» is the kind of government used in Athens. As a noun it names people: «Athenians» are the people who lived in Athens. Notice the capital A, because it comes from a place name.
explain: Look at the words around it. «Once a year Athenians could vote to send a too-powerful politician away for ten years» tells you that Athenians were citizens who voted. Ask what would fit: a word for people from one city, not all Greeks. Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
fact: Athenian means belonging to or coming from Athens, the capital city of Greece.
fact: An Athenian is a person who lived in ancient Athens or lives in Athens today.
fact: «Athenian democracy» means the way citizens of Athens ran their city by voting.
fact: An ostrakon was a piece of broken pottery used in a vote, and «ostracism» is the name for sending a politician away this way.
exercise: «In 490 BC the Athenians beat a Persian army at Marathon.» Who are the Athenians here? | Runners who carried news | Soldiers who lived in a castle | People from Persia | *People from Athens
exercise: What does Athenian mean? | A famous long-distance runner | *Belonging to or coming from Athens | Belonging to ancient Persia | A kind of old pottery
exercise: «Once a year Athenians could vote to send a too-powerful politician away for ten years.» What is this kind of vote called? | Athenian | Persian | *Ostracism | Marathon
test: In «the Athenian army», Athenian describes the army. What kind of word is it? | Adverb | Verb | Noun | *Adjective
test: «Stories often compare Athenians with Spartans.» In this sentence, what are the Athenians? | A kind of vote | A place | A type of pottery | *People
exam: What was an ostrakon in Athens? | A marble statue of a famous thinker | A gold coin used to pay soldiers | *A broken piece of pottery used in a vote | A long race to carry news
